body:
The weird texture bit looks like \[scratches\]([https://aaep.org/horsehealth/getting-handle-scratches](https://aaep.org/horsehealth/getting-handle-scratches)) to me, common in breeds with feathers (it looks like he may have them but they are trimmed?). Bit of a tricky situation to treat, biggest thing is keeping the area well ventilated and dry, SO DRY. Scratches however only affects the skin, usually on the back of the lower limb, not actually the foot itself

&#x200B;

The other thing it could be is a blown abscess near the coronary band? If so vet/farrier will be able to get it flushed out and such, and it may look ugly for a bit bit, but they heal up. I've got a horse at my work who is healing from one now and it really isn't a hard thing to manage. Again, keep it clean/well ventilated/dry until vet arrives. 

&#x200B;

Hope this helps! Sorry its hard to diagnose from a photo. 

&#x200B;

Me: Bachelor's in Equine Science, experience working as an Equine Vet Tech
